            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I looked into this, but can't find a coherent rule without regressing other things.\n\n> a mapping that simply logs some value in a Lua table or adds extmark somewhere\n\nA workaround is to iterate the cursor extmarks (`nvim.multicursor` namespace) and do stuff at each mark, instead of expecting multicursor to repeat side-effect-only actions.\n\nBeyond that, a no-arg form of `setrepeat()` #42069 could allow mappings to force cascade.",
