            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": ">A workaround is to iterate the cursor extmarks (`nvim.multicursor` namespace) and do stuff at each mark, instead of expecting multicursor to repeat side-effect-only actions.\n\nWe use this approach for [rotating selections](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/42283), but it currently has numerous limitations - see https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42270 and https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42258 for a few of them.",
